{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "TitanSystem local cash bags and counted custody",
    "version": "B02B6",
    "description": "Two workflows: durable preparation/dispatch/cancellation from existing audited withdrawal; independent receiver count/rejection and per-closed-turn coverage. All endpoints ManageCash; writes also POS contract. Reads require no current license. Store/device derived from session. Receiver must differ from sender AND drawer operator. Declared amount is null for other managers until receipt is committed; never supplied in receive input. Same local SQLite only, no remote-delivery guarantee. Each withdrawal has at most one active/received bag; canceled/rejected history remains and permits new bag with new seal. No cash/stock/journal movements created by custody. Count differences remain recorded, not automatic expenses or bank settlement. Operations return original snapshot on replay; GET bag returns current state. Operation receipts accessible only to their actor. GET rejects body; unknown/repeated query parameters rejected. Coverage is only audited local withdrawals, not all outflows or a bank balance; only closed original drawer operator with ManageCash. B02B12: supplier_paid_cents classifica sangrias vinculadas a fornecedor e sai de unassigned; supplier_returned_cents informativo,nao subtrair da sangria original nem somar de novo ao caixa. Devolucao tem suprimento proprio. Sangria com qualquer historico de malote nao pode virar pagamento."
  },
